{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: f4f9ef0c38844956aafa21135cd3cfd7343afedf on request/url-observation-host-binding, one commit over main e3ad5f92, four changed paths, all four exact-path artifacts live at that head (normaliser 7ac59949 is the behaviour basis and carries review.md, checks.json and the before-control log; the Stage 1 note e03254d8 is the lane's newest report), checkout clean, commit rests on request #4086.\n\nReproduced at the head: all eleven CI gates green (root and jsonataddl test, race and vet; module boundary; root module; both vulnerability scans; demo; clean checkout). Mutation control: with the e3ad5f92 normaliser overlaid, TestURLReputationNormalizerActualAuthorityHost and TestURLReputationNormalizerLongUserinfo fail; restored to exact bytes. Beyond the 56 committed cases I ran 16 further inputs through the evaluator (double at-sign with either host claimed, percent-encoded at-sign lookalike, host-with-port claim, IPv6 in userinfo, at-sign in a query with no path, uppercase percent escapes, trailing dot both ways, leading-zero port, control characters in the path, wildcard host, bare at-sign) and an independent read-only pass ran about 40 more including every binary-search boundary (userinfo lengths 0 to 700, 4095 to 4097, 65535 to 65537, 131071 to 131073, 200001, 250000, 261214): the first at-sign offset was exact in every case and no input bound a host the URL does not name. Refusals are ineffective with no event.\n\nArchitecture: bundle fold, its test and two documents; the typed normaliser and pipeline contracts, tables, exports and runtime are unchanged; no activation or continuation eligibility is claimed. Security: the actual authority host is bound after valid userinfo, colon-before-at and numeric-port-before-at spoofs refuse, prefix lookalikes, multiple at-signs, invalid escapes, whitespace, control characters and backslashes in the authority refuse, IPv6 is matched structurally with the port outside the brackets, and observed_full is stored exactly. Simplification: the 18-step search uses only allow-listed functions and is the smallest construction that locates the first at-sign without a new evaluator capability; the IPv6 expression is long but is the standard RFC 3986 form and is tested at every compression position.\n\nTwo non-blocking limitations, both pre-existing rather than introduced here, for the Stage 3 request to carry: (1) hosts are compared after Go lowercasing, not IDNA mapping, so http://İ.com/ with host i.com is accepted although UTS 46 maps that name to xn--i-9bb.com, and fullwidth digits are stored unmapped; the capture adapter should emit the IDNA ASCII host and the companion should match exclusions on that form. (2) An accepted observation whose URL is within about 350 bytes of the 256 KiB input cap fails with an output-size evaluation error, which the projection records as a gap rather than the documented eventless refusal; harmless in practice, but the README's refusal promise does not hold in that band.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:e03254d8f77335e0564916250da2190999094a13","head":"f4f9ef0c38844956aafa21135cd3cfd7343afedf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:5fe93a14e29de7c00faa11c2076ad49b40586d50\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:5fe93a14e29de7c00faa11c2076ad49b40586d50","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:3b4fcc38efc8d3358a16f97cb4ae13f2ab12c48e, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:5fe93a14e29de7c00faa11c2076ad49b40586d50, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:66840611fa175557bbabeea509452e76eafc2904, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:7ac59949726f2e790f09ee73a822233f5b93e213, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:909b5dd2f59257b4b07dcb3a699007295a5f3